  {
   "key": "scene_02",
   "text": "Going in, the form was lopsided. Bayern: four wins and a draw, including 2-0 away at Atlético Madrid. Köln: one win, two draws, two defeats, the latest a 1-2 loss at home to Bayer Leverkusen. Köln's coach is René Wagner, 37, in his first job as a head coach. For years he was Steffen Baumgart's assistant. He took over in March, when Lukas Kwasniok was sacked, kept Köln up, and was given the job until 2028. In the FC Bayern preview he asked: \"Other teams have already taken points off them in Munich – so why not us?\" His plan, per Geissblog.koeln: fast transitions, and expect Bayern to push them back. Both were short of players. Bayern were without Luis Díaz, Alphonso Davies, Ismael Saibari and Serge Gnabry. Köln were without five, including Thijs Dallinga.",
   "url": "https://media.viewmax.io/users/7RRunw8K5Hq1WuIqMTzGxHdTQZ5z8lPX/voiceover/ec406c38-0da4-454c-8be4-3e0298c191ed.wav",
