  {
   "key": "scene_07",
   "text": "Now the part the score hides. Expected goals, or xG, is a model built on many past shots: distance, angle, foot or head, type of pass. It says how often a chance like that is scored. FotMob gives Köln 1.99 xG and Bayern 1.07. Every Köln shot came from inside the box. Most of Bayern's 17 did not. Köln then missed 3 of their 4 big chances. Urbig saved 0.63 goals more than an average keeper would. Our reading: the draw owes something to Köln's finishing and something to Bayern's goalkeeper. Replay these chances 20,000 times, and Köln win 64 of every 100. Bayern win 14.",
