  {
   "key": "scene_09",
   "text": "The lesson is simple. Holding the ball is not the same as making chances that matter. And a compact side that breaks fast can cost the ball-holders points. For context, Leicester in 2015/16 averaged 42.5 percent possession and won the league with compact defending and direct attacks, in StatsBomb data. Köln had 28 percent here. Before the match, Wagner said Köln would need some luck. The numbers suggest the luck went Bayern's way. Was the draw fair? Tell us below, and subscribe for the next match.",
